@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+# v682 — Choosing a different AI provider
+
+Status: built and tested on the development branch. **Not live.** Releasing it needs the owner's approval.
+
+## What it does
+
+Until v681, every AI request went to Google Gemini. From v682, **Settings → "AI model provider — advanced"** lets you choose one of:
+
+| Choice | What you enter |
+|---|---|
+| Google Gemini (default) | Nothing new. This works exactly as before. |
+| OpenAI | API key, plus a fast model name (and an optional stronger one) |
+| Anthropic (Claude) | API key, plus a fast model name (and an optional stronger one) |
+| Other OpenAI-compatible service | Service address (for example https://openrouter.ai/api/v1, https://api.groq.com/openai/v1, https://api.deepseek.com/v1 or a local http://localhost:11434/v1), plus an API key and model names |
+
+- **Fast model:** does every job that Gemini Flash-Lite does today.
+- **Stronger model:** used only by the new generator's checker (the job Gemini Flash does). If you leave it empty, the fast model is used.
+- **Prices (optional):** US$ per million tokens. With them, the spend counter stays accurate. Without them, the cost shows as unknown.
+- **"Save & test connection":** sends one tiny request and shows the provider's answer.
+- **Switching back:** choose "Google Gemini (default)" and save.
+
+The same prompts, quality checks, retry rules and READY/NOT READY gates apply whatever provider is chosen. Nothing about vocabulary, SRS, belts or history changes. The only thing saved is the provider choice itself (`tt-ai-provider`, kept on the device).
+
+## How it works (for a developer)
+
+- There is still one request door, `geminiRequest`.
+  - With no provider chosen, it calls the unchanged Gemini sender.
+  - With a provider chosen, it calls `_aiProviderSend`, which:
+    - translates the request into that provider's format (OpenAI `chat/completions`, or Anthropic `messages`)
+    - translates the reply and its token counts back
+    - uses the same retry rules: 429 and 5xx are retried; a wrong key stops the run.
+- Model mapping: Gemini Flash-Lite → fast model; any other model → stronger model.
+- If a provider refuses a parameter (temperature, the token-limit field name, or JSON mode), that parameter is dropped and the request is repeated once.
+- Incomplete settings (no key, no model, or a bad address) never switch the provider. Gemini keeps working, and Settings says what is missing.
+
+## Evidence
+
+| Test | Result |
+|---|---|
+| `tests41.js`: request shapes, model mapping, cost from the provider's token counts, refused-parameter adaptation, 429 retry, 401 stop, key handling | 19/19 |
+| `tests41.js` E1–E3: a **full Daily lesson** sent as OpenAI requests (Japanese 74 requests, Mandarin 204), as Anthropic requests (same), and through a compatible service (Thai 208). Each gives exactly the same lesson as the Gemini path, with no request to Gemini. | pass |
+| `sandbox/browser_v682.js` (real page in Chromium): Settings panel, refusal of incomplete settings, connection test, the choice surviving a reload, Thai and Mandarin Daily going to the chosen provider, switching back to Gemini, Anthropic with no Gemini key, no learner data touched | 10/10 |
+| Default Gemini path | Unchanged. The 18 recorded live runs replay identically (tests39 A5), and the full suite passes. |
+
+These tests use a simulated provider. They prove the plumbing, not how good another model's lessons would be.
+
+## Not yet done
+
+- **No real call to another provider has been made.** This sandbox can only reach Google's servers, and only with the key sent as `x-goog-api-key`.
+  - Google also offers an OpenAI-format address (`…/v1beta/openai/`). It needs the key as `Authorization: Bearer`.
+  - If the owner adds that header to the sandbox secret, the "compatible" path can be tested for real against Gemini at a cost of a few cents.
+- **Quality on another model is unknown.** The prompts and checks were tuned on Flash-Lite. Compare a few lessons before relying on another provider.
+- **Keys entered in Settings stay on the device**, the same as the Gemini key.
+  - OpenAI and Anthropic allow direct calls from a browser. Anthropic needs a special header, which the app sends.
+  - Some other services block browser calls. If so, the connection test shows the error.
+
+## TL;DR
+
+v682 adds a provider choice under Settings: Gemini (the default, unchanged), OpenAI, Claude, or any OpenAI-compatible service. Tests sent complete lessons through each format and got lessons identical to Gemini's, and the real page works in a browser. No real call to another provider has been made yet, and how good lessons are on other models is unknown. It is not live until the owner approves.
